$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure A: Aldol reactions between aldehydes and methyl trimethylsilyl
dimethylketene acetal (2): To aldehyde (3.0 mmol) in a dry flask under N2
were added THF (anhydrous, 15 rnL), methyl trimethylsilyl dimethylketene
acetal (0.66 g, 3.60 mmol based on 95% purity) and carbene 5 (5 mg, 0.014
mmol). The mixture was stirred at 23 °C for 3 h. HC1 solution (1 N, 3 mL)
was added and the solution was stirred at 23 °C for 1 h. Saturated NaHCO3
aq solution (3 mL) and water (3 mL) were added. Dichloromethane (50 mL)
was added and the aqueous layer was extracted with dichloromethane (50
mL). Organic layers were combined and solvents were removed under vacuum
to give the crude residue, which was purified by silica gel flash
chromatography (ethyl acetate/hexanes) to give pure product Compound 6a
was prepared by using Procedure A and isolated by silica gel flash
chromatography (5-35% EtOAc/hexanes) in 77% yield. 1H NMR (CDC13, 400
MHz) δ 7.74-7.83 (m, 4H), 7.41-7.49 (m, 3H), 5.05 (d, J = 4.2 Hz, 1H),
3.72 (s, 3H), 3.28 (d, J = 4.2 Hz, 1H), 1.18 (s, 3H), 1.14 (s, 3H). 13C
NMR (CDC13, 100 MHz) δ 178.3, 137.5, 133.0, 132.8, 128.1, 127.6, 127.3,
126.7, 126.1, 126.0, 125.7, 78.8, 52.2, 48.0, 23.2, 19.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on catalyst and solvent
