$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of the aldehyde (9.2 g, 20.58 mmol), obtained above, in THF
(60 ml) was added TBS enol-ether of t-butylacetate (9.4 g, 41.7 mmol).
Then the reaction mixture was cooled to -78 °C and treated with BF3.Et2O
(2.83 ml, 22.5 mmol). After being stirred for 30 min at the same
temperature the reaction mixture was warmed up to 0 °C and quenched with
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution. Then it was extracted with EtOAc,
washed with water, brine, dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by column chromatography (SiO2, 2 to 3% Ethyl acetate in
petroleum ether eluant) afforded 20 (9.6 g, 76%) as a yellowish oil.
(3S,4R,5R,6R)-tert-butyl
5-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-7-(tertbutyldiphenylsilyloxy)-
3-hydroxy-4,6-dimethylheptanoate (20),Yield(9.6 g, 76%). Rf = 0.5 (SiO2,
4.5% EtOAc in petroleum ether). [α]D 29 = -3.9 (c = 2.40, CHCl3); 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 200 MHz): δ 7.67-7.59 (m, 4H), 7.41-7.31 (m, 6H), 3.9 (q, J = 5.4
Hz, 1H), 3.81 (t, J = 4.1 Hz, 1H), 3.68 (dd, J = 9.9, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 3.41
(dd, J = 10.4, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 2.93 (s, 1H), 2.3(d, J = 6.2 Hz, 2H), 2.01(m,
1H), 1.62(m, 1H)1.46 (s, 9H), 1.06 (s, 9H), 0.09 (d, J = 7.1Hz, 6H), 0.84
(s, 9H), 0.04 (s, 3H), -0.03 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 172.4,
135.6, 133.7, 129.5, 127.6, 80.9, 74.8, 70.3, 66.2, 40.9, 40.9, 28.1,
26.9, 26.0, 19.3, 18.3, 13.7, 9.7, -3.8, -4.2; IR (neat): 3410, 2926,
2853, 1718, 1465, 1427, 1367, 1253, 1153, 1108, 833, 702 cm-1; MS (ESI):
m/z (%) 615 (100) [M + H]+, 637 (95) [M + Na]+; HRMS (ESI) calculated for
C35H58O5NaSi2 [M + Na]+ m/z 637.3720, found 637.3750.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
