$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of aldehyde (910mg, 1.7 mmol) and silylenolether (1.58g, 3.6
mmol) was azeotropically dried with toluene several times before
dissolved in anhydrous DCM (25ml). The solution was cooled to -78 °C and
freshly distilled BF3OEt2 (2.2 ml, 18 mmol) was added dropwise. The
reaction mixture was allowed to stir at -78 °C overnight beforeit was
quenched by addition of saturated NaHCO3 (30 ml) at -78 °C and extracted
with EtOAc. Combined organic layers were washed with brine and dried over
Na2SO4. After concentration, the residue was purified by FC (EtOAc/Hexane
1/9) to give product as a colorless oil, yield 0.96 g, 76%. [α]20D = +
28.59 (c = 0.1,DCM); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.34-7.26 (m, 5H), 6.30 (s, 1H),
4.48 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.44 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.36 (ddd, J = 2.5,
5.0, 12.5 Hz, 1H), 4.31-4.27 (m, 1H), 4.05 (dd, J = 2.5, 7.5 Hz, 1H),
3.49 (dd, J = 5.5, 8.0 Hz, 2H), 3.24 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.89 (dd, J =
2.5, 16.0 Hz, 1H), 2.78-2.71 (m, 2H), 2.08 (s, 3H), 1.83-1.69 (m, 2H),
1.62-1.54 (m, 5H), 1.35-1.25 (m, 8H), 1.18-1.05 (m, 42 H), 0.86 (s, 9H),
0.05 (s, 3H), 0.04 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 217.4, 163.1, 159.0, 157.7,
141.4, 138.5, 128.6, 127.9, 118.3, 109.7, 78.3, 74.0, 73.2, 67.9, 67.5,
53.8, 42.9, 41.7, 34.7, 29.9, 26.2, 22.3, 20.2, 18.5, 18.3, 18.2, 17.9,
13.5, 13.4, 12.0, 9.6, -3.7, -3.8; MS (ES) calculated for C52H91O8Si3 [M
+ H]+: 927.60, found 927.73; C52H90NaO8Si3 [M + Na]+: 949.58, found
949.68;
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, dr=15:1
