$DATUM Reagents: cyclohexanone (70 mg, 0.71 mmol), 2a (167 mg, 1.1 mmol), and
Bi(OTf)3•4H2O (25 mg, 0.036 mmol). The mixture was stirred at -45 °C for
3 h and then quenched according to the typical procedure. The crude
product was then purified on silica gel (20% ethyl acetate/hexanes) to
afford 97 mg (75%) of 3m as a white solid. mp 51 °C; Rf = 0.18 (20% ethyl
acetate/hexanes); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.50 (dq, J = 5.9, 0.9 Hz,
1H); 6.17 (m, 1H), 4.85 (m, 1H), 2.12 (br s, 1H), 1.40-1.65 (m, 9H),
1.16-1.25 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 173.6, 154.1, 122.9,
89.8, 72.8, 33.8, 33.5, 25.6, 21.3; IR (KBr): 3459, 1810 cm-1; HRMS:
Calcd for C10H14O3 (M+) 182.0943, found 182.0947.
