$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (R,E)-Methyl 5-Hydroxy-8-methyl-3-oxoundeca-8,10-dienoate (7).
Titanium(IV) isopropoxide (0.07mL, 0.24mmol) was added slowly to a
suspension of (S)-BINOL (0.14g, 0.48mmol) and activated 4Å molecular
sieves (1.06g) in THF (12mL). The mixture was kept stirring at rt for 1h
and was then cooled to -78°C. The compound 1 (0.38g, 3.06mmol) was added
dropwisely, followed, after 30min, by silyloxydiene 2 (2.36g, 9.09mmol)
in dry THF (3mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at -78°C for another
2h and then warmed to rt. At rt, the mixture was stirred for 16h. Later,
after cooling the mixture to -78°C again, TFA (1.21mL) was added and the
solution was warmed to rt. After stirring at rt for 1h, the reaction
mixture was diluted with EtOAc (10mL), a saturated aqueous NaHCO3
solution (6mL) was added slowly, and the mixture stirred until the
evolution of gas ceased. Subsequently, the mixture was extracted with
EtOAc (3×20mL). The combined organic layer was washed with brine and
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was evaporated under reduced
pressure, and the residue was purified by silica-gel column
chromatography (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate = 10:1). Compound 7 (0.55g,
75%) as a colorless oily liquid. [α]D 25 = -16:3 (c = 1.5, CHCl3); 1H NMR
δ (400MHz, CDCl3), 6.55 (ddd, J =17.2, 10.4, 10.4Hz, 1H), 5.87 (d, J
=10.8Hz, 1H), 5.10 (d, J=16.8Hz, 1H), 4.99 (d, J =10.0Hz, 1H), 4.12-4.01
(m, 1H), 3.74 (s, 3H), 3.49 (s, 2H), 2.79-2.68 (m, 2H), 2.25- 2.07 (m,
2H), 1.75 (s, 3H), 1.68-1.56 (m, 2H). 13C NMR δ (CDCl3, ppm) 203.4,
167.3, 138.6, 133.1, 125.9, 115.1, 67.1, 52.4, 49.6, 35.6, 34.4, 16.6.
HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C13H20O4Na [M+ Na]+ 263.1254; found 263.1255.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mukaiyama Aldol addition, ee = 86%, molecular sieves used (stage 1)
