$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7. A general procedure for 4b·L2-catalyzed Mukaiyama aldol reaction with
ketones: Freshly distilled THF (5 mL) was injected at room temperature
under nitrogen into pyrex Schrenk tube containing sodium phenoxide (5b)
(2.9 mg, 0.025 mmol) and 1,2-bis(diphenylphosphoryl)benzene (L) (23.9 mg,
0.050 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 10 min at that temperature, and
then this colorless solution was cooled to –78 °C and stirred for 5 min
at that temperature. methyl
2-methyl-3,3-diphenyl-3-(trimethylsilyloxy)propanoate (3e). 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ – 0.12 (s, 9H), 1.15 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 3.55 (s, 3H),
3.74 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.20-7.40 (m, 10H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
1.8, 14.4, 48.4, 51.3, 82.7, 127.0, 127.1, 127.5, 127.6, 128.3, 128.5,
144.4, 174.1. IR(film) 2950, 1746, 1446, 1249, 1196, 1157, 1089, 1070
cm-1. HRMS(FAB+) calcd for C20H26NaO3Si [M+Na]+ 365.1549, found 365.1545.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
