$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Catalysis Experiment (Table 3, Entry 1);
Typical Procedure The complex [FeCl2 8] (0.010 g, 0.018 mmol) was
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL), and in another flask AgSbF6 (0.012 g, 0.036
mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL). The solution of AgSbF6 was added
to the solution of the metal complex and stirred at r.t. for 1 h. In a
third flask, 4-ethylbenzaldehyde (0.049 g, 0.362 mmol) and the silane 5
(0.085 g, 0.543 mmol) were mixed in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) and stirred at r.t. for
3.5 h. The solution of the activated catalyst was then filtered through
Celite® directly into the solution of the substrates, and the color of
the solution turned to reddish. The reaction mixture was stirred
overnight, then filtered through a pad of silica gel (3.5 cm). The silica
gel was washed with CH2Cl2 (about 2 mL) and the filtrate was
concentrated. The yellow residue that was obtained was 95% pure (1H NMR
spectroscopy), and any further purification gave only decomposition
products, and elution with extremely nonpolar solvents like hexanes also
yielded small amounts of silyl impurities (about 5%). Table 4 entry 3 The
aldol reaction of 4-ethylbenzaldehyde (0.023 g, 0.170 mmol) was carried
out with tert-butyldimethyl(1-phenylvinyloxy)silane (6, 0.060 g, 0.255
mmol) with the activated catalyst [8Fe(μCl)3FeCl3] (0.006 g, 0.0085 mmol
catalyst with 0.006 g, 0.017 mmol AgSbF6) for 3.5 h. The product was
obtained as colorless oil (0.045 g, 0.123 mmol, 73%).3 1H-NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 8.00-7.94 (m, 2 H, Ar), 7.58-7.55 (m, 1 H, Ar), 7.54-7.43 (m,
2 H, Ar), 7.37-7.34 (m, 2 H, Ar), 7.19-7.17 (m, 2 H, Ar), 5.36 (dd, 2 J
HH = 8.9 Hz, 3 J HH = 3.8 Hz, 1 H, CHOSi t Bu2CH3), 3.60 (dd, 2 J HH =
15.1Hz, 3 J HH = 8.9 Hz, 1 H, CHH’CO), 2.95 (d, 2 J HH =15.1 Hz, 3 J HH =
3.8 Hz, 1 H, CHH’CO), 2.67 (q, 2 J HH =7.6 Hz, 2 H, CH2CH3), 1.25 (t, 2 J
HH =6.6 Hz, 3 H, CH2CH3), 0.77 (s, 9 H, C(CCH3)3), –0.07 (s, 3 H, SiCH3),
–0.16 (s, 3 H, SiCH3). 13C{1H}-NMR (75.41 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 199.0 (C=O),
143.5, 142.3, 137.9, 133.2, 128.73, 128.67, 127.9, 126.0, 72.4, 50.1,
28.7, 25.9, 18.3, 15.7, –4.5 (s, SiCH3), –5.1 (s, SiCH3’). IR (neat):
1685 (C=O) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New bis(imino)pyridine complexes of iron(II) and iron(III), and their
catalytic activity in the Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
