$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Catalytic Aldol
Addition. To a solution of MAD or MABR in dichloromethane was added a
trialkylsilyl sulfonate at -78 °C under argon. Then, silyl enol ether 3a
or 3b and the aldehyde or ketone were added dropwise in this order at the
temperature. After stirring for a given reaction time, the reaction
mixture was poured into 1N HCl and stirred vigorously for several minutes
to complete cleavage of the silyl ether, then extracted with ether. The
extract was, after drying over MgSO4 and being concentrated, subjected to
column chromatography on silica gel (ethyl acetate/hexane as eluent).
Entry: 7; Yield: 74%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on catalyst, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, MABR
co-catalyst prepared and used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Remarkable Enhancement of Catalyst Activity of Trialkylsilyl Sulfonates
on the Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction: A New Approach Using Bulky
Organoaluminum Cocatalysts
