$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure A (Suitable for
Liquid Aldehydes). To an emulsion of benzaldehyde (2a) (0.08 mL, 0.80
mmol) in 1.5 mL of brine/MeOH (1:0.5 mixture), under sonication at 38-40
°C, was slowly added a solution of N-Boc-2-(trimethylsilyloxy)pyrrole
(1a) (100 mg, 0.40 mmol) dissolved in MeOH (0.5 mL). The reaction, kept
under sonication at the same temperature for 3 h, was cooled to room
temperature, then added with ice, and the resulting slurry mixture was
extracted with EtOAc (3 × 20 mL). The organic layers were collected,
dried with MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The diastereomeric
ratio of the addition products was determined to be 83.3/16.7 (anti/syn)
by 1H NMR analysis of the crude reaction mixture. The crude residue,
dissolved in anhydrous ethanol, was filtered through a Whatman Anotop 10
LC filter, and purified by semipreparative HPLC (CN-10 μm, 250 × 10 mm,
hexane/anhydrous EtOH 90:10, flow rate 3.0 mL/min, detection at 254 nm,
Rt anti-3a = 12.79 min), yielding major isomer anti-3a.
(5R*,1'S*)-N-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)-5-[hydroxy(naphthalen-1-yl)methyl]-1H-pyrrol-2(5H)-one
(anti-3d). (100 mg, 74%) as a glassy solid. 1H NMR: (300 MHz, CDCl3) 8.35
(d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H, Ar), 7.91 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, Ar), 7.84 (d, J = 8.2
Hz, 1H, Ar), 7.73 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H, Ar), 7.50-7.59 (m, 3H, Ar), 6.79
(dd, J = 6.1, 2.0 Hz, 1H, H4), 6.32 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H, H1'), 6.15 (dd, J
= 6.3, 1.7 Hz, 1H, H3), 5.11 (ddd, J = 2.1, 2.0, 2.0 Hz, 1H, H5), 1.71
(s, 9H, t-Bu, Boc). 13C NMR: (75 MHz, CDCl3) 163.2 (Cq, C2), 150.6 (Cq,
Boc), 147.1 (CH, C4), 135.6 (Cq, Ar), 133.8 (Cq, Ar), 130.2 (Cq, Ar),
129.3 (CH, Ar), 128.7 (CH, Ar), 128.4 (CH, C3), 126.8 (CH, Ar), 126.0
(CH, Ar), 125.7 (CH, Ar), 123.7 (CH, Ar), 123.1 (CH, Ar), 77.4 (Cq, t-Bu,
Boc), 68.2 (CH, C1'), 67.3 (CH, C5), 28.6 (3C, CH3 , t-Bu, Boc). MS:
(ESI, 50 eV) 340.1 (M+H)+; 362.1 (M+Na)+ Analysis.: C20H21NO4 (339.39)
Calcd: C, 70.78; H, 6.24; N, 4.13 Found: C, 70.70; H, 6.30; N, 4.10.
