$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Mukaiyama Aldol
Reactions Reported in Tables 1 and 2. Preparation of ent-9. To a cold
(-78 °C) stirring solution of (S)-Garner’s aldehyde ent-83 (4.6 g, 20
mmol), 2,6-di-tert-butyl-4-methylpyridine (16 g, 80 mmol) and CH2Cl2 (70
mL) was added dropwise BF3 ·Et2O (8.9 mL, 70 mmol). After stirring for 30
min at -78°C, a solution of freshly prepared siloxyindole 7 (5.40 g, 10.0
mmol) and CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was added dropwise. After stirring for 2 h at
-78 °C and 14 h at -50 °C, the reaction was poured into water (100 mL),
the phases were separated, and the aqueous phase was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3x80 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried (MgSO4) and concentrated to afford a yellowish oil. Purification of
this oil by column chromatography (20/1 to 3/1 hexanes/EtOAc) provided
ent-9 (6.07 g, 92%) as a colorless foam. An analytical sample was
obtained by HPLC (85:15 hexanes-ethyl acetate, 20 mL/min):
4-{[1-Benzyl-3-(4-methoxyphenyl)-2-oxo-2,3-dihydro-1H-indol-3-yl]
hydroxymethyl}-2,2-dimethyl-oxazolidine-3-carboxylic acid tert-butyl
ester (14b). According to the general procedure, siloxyindole 13b (52 mg,
0.12 mmol) and ent-8 (55 mg, 0.24 mmol) were condensed to afford a
yellowish oil, which upon purification by HPLC (87/13 hexanes/ethyl
acetate; 20 mL/min) gave 14b (48 mg, 73%) as a colorless oil. colorless
oil: [α]D 27 +27.3 (c = 0.49, CHCl3); IR (film) 3464, 3033, 2925, 1690,
1611 cm-1; HRMS (CI) calcd for C33H39N2O6 (M+H): 559.2808; found:
559.2794.4
