$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Catalytic Aldol Addition. To a solution of MAD
or MABR in dichloromethane was added a trialkylsilyl sulfonate at -78 °C
under argon. Then, silyl enol ether 3a or 3b and the aldehyde or ketone
were added dropwise in this order at the temperature. After stirring for
a given reaction time, the reaction mixture was poured into 1N HCl and
stirred vigorously for several minutes to complete cleavage of the silyl
ether, then extracted with ether. The extract was, after drying over
MgSO4 and being concentrated, subjected to column chromatography on
silica gel (ethyl acetate/hexane as eluent). Aldol adduct in the yields
as shown in Tables 1 and 2. The isomeric ratio was determined by 300 MHz
1H NMR and capillary GLC analysis by comparison with authentic samples.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on catalyst, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, MABR
co-catalyst prepared and used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Remarkable Enhancement of Catalyst Activity of Trialkylsilyl Sulfonates
on the Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction: A New Approach Using Bulky
Organoaluminum Cocatalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Oishi, Masataka; Aratake, Seiji; Yamamoto, Hisashi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (1998), 120(32), 8271-8272

