$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction
of Methyl Trimethylsilyl Dimethylketene Acetal and
2-(Trimethylsiloxy)furan. To a 10 mL vial equipped with a stir bar was
added 22.15 mg (2.5 mol %) of alumatrane dimer 2 in a glovebox.
Acetonitrile (5 mL) followed by 1 mmol of the corresponding aldehyde were
added to the vial, and then the reaction mixture was stirred for 30 min
at room temperature to form the aldehyde-alumatrane adduct. The
corresponding silyl enol ether (1.2 mmol) was added under inert
atmosphere and then the reaction was continued for the allotted time as
recorded in the tables. Then 3 mL of 2 N hydrochloric acid solution was
added and the reaction mixture was stirred for an additional 3 hat room
temperature. The reaction mixture was extracted with methylene chloride
and dried over Na2SO4, the solution was filtered and dried on a rotovap
apparatus, and then the crude product was purified by column
chromatography (EtOAc:hexanes=1:9).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, syn:anti=1:4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalysis of Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions by a Tricyclic Aluminum Alkoxide
Lewis Acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Raders, Steven M.; Verkade, John G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(15), 5417-5428

