$DATUM We investigated the use of this direct method employing diene 4 (Scheme
1). Although preliminary experiments using this reagent afforded good
yields in additions to aldehydes using BF3.OEt2 as Lewis acid, the use of
reagent 4 in catalytic asymmetric additions using BITIP catalysis was not
promising. Rf 0.46 (20% acetone/hexanes); [α]D 20 -13.7 (c = 1.095,
CHCl3); 500 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.42 – 7.36 (m, 4H), 7.34 – 7.29 (m,
1H), 6.75 (dd, J = 7.3, 6.9 Hz, 1H), 4.85 – 4.82 (m, 1H), 2.67 (ddd, J =
15.4, 7.7, 7.7 Hz, 1H), 2.61 – 2.56 (m, 1H), 2.10 (bs, 1H), 1.79 (s, 3H),
1.49 (s, 9H); 125 MHz 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 195.0, 143.9, 139.3, 135.1, 128.8
(2), 128.1, 125.9 (2), 73.6, 47.7, 38.7, 30.1 (3), 12.7; 125 MHz DEPT
(CDCl3) δ CH3: 30.1 (3), 12.7. CH2: 38.7. CH: 135.1, 128.8 (2), 128.1,
125.9 (2), 73.6. C: 195.0, 143.9, 139.3, 47.7; IR (neat) 3424, 3081,
3062, 3033, 2995, 2963, 2915, 2867, 1950, 1886, 1808, 1759, 1650, 1494,
1477, 1487, 1454, 1363, 1307, 1259, 1198, 1160, 1079, 1051, 1027, 987,
954, 899, 864 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C16H22O2S: C, 69.02; H, 7.96. Found:
C, 68.84; H, 8.17.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 4A mol. sieves used
