$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2. General procedure for the synthesis of
β-hydroxy carboxylic esters To a solution of the freshly prepared
catalyst (S)-1c (0.296 mmol, 20 mol%) at -40 °C were successively added a
solution of triphenylphospine oxide (0.616 mmol, 171 mg, 0.5 equiv) in
toluene (2 mL) and aldehyde (1.23 mmol, 1.0 equiv) (solid aldehydes were
added as solution in 0.5 mL of toluene) to the mixture. After 15 min
stirring at -40°C, (1-methoxy-2-methyl- propenyloxy)-trimethylsilane
(1.47 mmol, 300 μL, 1.2 equiv) was added slowly for 20 min to the
reaction mixture. The reaction was monitored by TLC. After the reaction
time indicated in Table 2, it was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3
solution (2 mL), washed with H2O (10 mL) and extracted with EA (3 × 20
mL). The combined organic phase was washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4) and
the removal of the solvent under vacuum provided the crude product. The
resulting crude mixture was dissolved in 2 ml of dry THF and stirred with
tetrabutylammonium fluoride (1.23 mL, 1.23 mmol, 1 M solution in THF) at
0°C for 15 min. Removal of the solvent under vacuum provided the crude
product. Purification by flash column chromatography afforded the pure
product. (R)- Methyl 2,2-dimethyl-3-hydroxynonanoate (Table 2, entry 13).
colorless oil. Rf = 0.28 (EtOAc/hexane = 1/6), 72% yield, 86% ee,[α]D20
+60.94 (c 0.318, MeOH). GC condition: γ-TA column, T = 120°C, F = 0.5, t1
= 35.30 min (minor) and t2 = 36.70 min (major). IR (neat): υmax 3700,
2998, 2852, 1725, 1467, 1271, 1140, 1080, 1038, 966, 863; 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3): δ 3.70 (s, 3H), 3.62- 3.56 (m, 1H); 2.47 (br s, 1H); 1.71-
1.50 (m, 2H); 1.48-1.20 (m, 8H); 1.18 (s, 3H); 1.17 (s, 3H); 0.88 (t, 3H,
J = 6.9 Hz); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 178.4, 76.8, 52.0, 47.3, 31.9,
31.7, 29.3, 26.7, 22.7, 22.3, 20.4, 14.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama Aldol reaction (stage 1-2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
