$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the asymmetric
Mukaiyama-Type Aldol Reaction: A flame-dried Schlenk tube under argon
atmosphere was charged with Cu(OTf)2 (0.025 mmol) and sulfoximine 4
(0.026 mmol). Then, dry toluene (1.5 mL) was added, and the resulting
deep green solution was stirred for 30 min at room temperature. The
reaction mixture was cooled to reaction temperature. Subsequently,
pyruvate ester 5 (0.25 mmol), enol silyl ether 6 (0.30 mmol), and
2,2,2-trifluoroethanol (0.30 mmol) were added. After stirring for the
indicated period of time, the solvent was removed, and the product was
purified by flash chromatography (PE:Et2O˜1:1). The absolute
configurations of 7a was determined by measuring HPLC and compared to the
literature values5 of the corresponding enantiomers. By using (S,S)-4,
the (R)-configurated product 7a was formed in preference. For the other
products it was assigned in analogy.
(R)-Methyl-[2-hydroxy-2-methyl-4-oxo-4-(1-naphthyl)]-butanoate (7c): The
product was prepared according to the general procedure. It was obtained
in 70% yield after flash chromatography. [α]D25 = -26.7 (c = 1.38,
CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.54 (s, 3H), 3.44 (d, J= 17.4 Hz,
1H), 3.77 (d, J= 17.3 Hz, 1H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 4.11 (bs, 1H), 7.50-7.62 (m,
3H), 7.86-7.94 (m, 2H), 8.00-8.03 (m, 1H), 8.63-8.65 (m, 1H) ppm; 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 26.5, 51.0, 52.8, 73.1, 124.2, 125.6, 126.6, 128.2,
128.4, 128.5, 130.0, 133.5, 133.9, 134.8, 176.6, 202.9 ppm; MS (70 eV,
EI): m/z (%) = 272.0 (19) [M], 231.0 (19), 213.0 (12), 155.0 (100), 126.9
(33); IR (kap): ν = 3515, 1740, 1677, 1509, 1453, 1215, 1179, 1113, 802,
759, cm-1; elemental analysis (%) calcd for C16H16O4: C 70.57, H 5.92;
found: C 70.87, H 5.78. The enantiomer ratio was determined by HPLC
analysis using a Chiralcel OBH column (flow rate 0.7 mL/min,
heptane/i-PrOH: 93/7, λ = 210 nm, 20 °C); tr = 75.5 min [major], tr =
87.5 min [minor]; 90% ee.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 82% ee, reaction on ice cooling gave lower yield and
enantioselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
