$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of compound 7b: To a solution of aldehyde 6 (2.71 g, 12.83
mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (100 mL) was slowly added TiCl4 (7.10 mL, 1 M in
CH2Cl2, 7.10 mmol) at -78 °C, and the mixture was stirred at the same
temperature for 30 min. To this solution was added a solution of
vinylketene silyl N,O-acetal 5 (2.50 g, 6.45 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) at
-78 °C, and the reaction mixture was warmed up to room temperature and
stirred for 2 h. The reaction mixture was quenched by addition of a
saturated aqueous Rochelle's salt (80 mL), and the mixture was extracted
with ethyl acetate (3 x 60 mL). The combined organic layers were
sequentially washed with a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (2 x 60
mL) and brine (60 mL), and then dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent
was removed under vacuum, and the residue was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel (hexane/ethyl acetate/CH2Cl2 = 4:1:1) to
give product 7b. Colorless oil, yield 2.870 g, 92%. Rf = 0.25
(hexane/ethyl acetate = 2:1). IR νmax (neat) / cm-1:3506(br), 2931, 1785,
1685, 1531, 1352, 1298, 1217, 1048, 995, 773, 762, 703. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.42 - 7.25 (m, 5H), 7.25 - 7.13 (m, 2H), 6.02 (dd, J = 9.3, 1.4
Hz, 1H), 5.25 (dd, J = 3.9, 3.8 Hz, 1H), 4.89 - 4.78 (m, 1H), 4.32 (dd, J
= 8.8, 8.7 Hz, 1H), 4.20 (dd, J = 9.0, 6.5 Hz, 1H), 3.87 (s, 3H), 3.82
(s, 3H), 3.34 - 3.19 (m, 2H), 3.13 - 2.98 (m, 1H), 2.90 (dd, J = 13.6,
8.8 Hz), 2.08 (d, J = 1.3 Hz, 3H), 0.85 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (101
MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.3, 155.0, 154.2, 143.8, 143.5, 143.2, 139.3, 134.7,
130.2, 129.4, 128.9, 127.4, 119.0, 108.6, 70.9, 66.3, 62.5, 55.9, 55.0,
37.9, 37.4, 13.4, 12.4. HRMS (ESI): calcd for C25H28N2NaO8 [M + Na+]
507.1738; found 507.1734. [α]D20 °C = +17 (1.0, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, slow addition of titanium tetrachloride/DCM stage 1,
chelation-controlled vinylogous Mukaiyama aldol reaction, key step
