$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of aldehyde (0.8 mmol) in
propionitrile (0.32 mL) was added over 10 min to a mixed solution of the
silyl enol ether (0.96 mmol) and 2d (0.08 mmol) in propionitrile (0.65
mL). 2-(α- Hydroxybenzyl)cyclohexanone (Table 2), yield 99%. 1H NMR, 13C
NMR, and IR spectroscopic data are in agreement with those reported in
the literatures.1,3 The syn/anti ratio was determined by 1H NMR
spectroscopy: 1H NMR (CDCl3 , 300 MHz) δ 3.01 (d, J=3.0 Hz, 1H, OH (syn
isomer)), 3.97 (d, J=1.0 Hz, 1H, OH (anti isomer)), 4.78 (m, 1H, CHOH
(anti isomer), 5.39 (m, 1H, CHOH (syn isomer)); The enantiomeric ratios
and the absolute configurations were determined by HPLC analysis (Daicel
OD-H column with hexane-i-PrOH=9:1, flow rate=0.5 mL/min):3 tR=14.3 (syn,
major enantiomer (2R, αR)), 15.8 (syn, minor enantiomer (2S , αS)), 17.8
(anti, minor enantiomer), 24.3 (anti, major enantiomer) min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative prepn. gave lower selectivity
