$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a stirred solution of the (S)-aldehyde 17 (4.0 g, 12.26 mmol) in 120
mL of dry CH2Cl2 at -95 °C (liquid N2 and acetone mixture), silyl enol
ether 18 prepared above was added followed by slow addition of BF3·Et2O
(1.82 mL, 14.7 mmol) at -95 °C. After stirring for 15 min at -95 °C and
the reaction mixture was placed in -78 °C cooling bath. After stirred for
30 min at -78 °C the reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3
(5 mL). After warming to RT the mixture was extracted with EtOAc (100 mL
× 3). The combined organic extracts were washed with water (40 mL), brine
(20 mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purification
by column chromatography (silica gel, 10% EtOAc in hexanes) gave
β-hydroxy ketone 19 (6.2 g, 92%) as an inseparable mixture of
diastereoisomers in the ratio 91:9. Excess silyl enol ether was recovered
as a methyl ketone. Rf : 0.3 (silica gel, 10% EtOAc in hexane); [α]D 27:
-7.5 (c 1.4, CHCl3); IR (neat): ν max 3436, 3049, 2956, 2858, 1698, 1471,
1390, 1256, 1098, 740 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.69-7.65 (m, 4H),
7.43-7.38 (m, 6H), 4.29-4.25 (m, 1H), 3.71-3.64 (m, 2H), 3.57 (s, 2H),
3.23 (bs, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H), 2.72 (dd, J = 17.9, 8.4 Hz, 1H), 2.65 (dd, J =
17.9, 4.1 Hz, 1H), 1.78-1.72 (m, 1H), 1.08 (s, 3H), 1.07 (s, 3H), 1.06
(s, 9H), 0.93 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.86 (s, 9H), 0.02 (s, 6H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 216.18, 135.74, 135.66, 134.88, 133.65, 133.52,
129.73, 127.76, 70.22, 68.71, 67.03, 49.86, 42.58, 40.01, 26.98, 26.64,
25.87, 21.46, 19.31, 18.25, 11.11, -5.54; HRMS (ESI): Calcd for
C32H53O4Si2 [M+H]+ 557.3483, found 557.3470.
