$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of aldehyde (0.8 mmol) in
propionitrile (0.32 mL) was added over 10 min to a mixed solution of the
silyl enol ether (0.96 mmol) and 2d (0.08 mmol) in propionitrile (0.65
mL). 1,5-Dipheny1-3-hydroxy-2-methyl-4-pentyn-1-one (Table 3), yield 92%.
1H NMR, 13C NMR, and IR spectroscopic data are in agreement with those
reported in the literature.1c The syn/anti ratio was determined by 'H NMR
spectroscopy: 1H NMR (CDCl3 , 300 MHz) δ 1.37 (d, J=7.1 Hz, 3H, CHCH3
(anti isomer)), 1.48 (d, J=7.1 Hz, 3H, CHCH3 (syn isomer)), 3.38 (d,
J=6.3 Hz, 1H, OH (anti isomer)), 3.46 (d, J=4.2 Hz, 1H, OH (syn isomer)),
4.96 (t, J=7.0 Hz, 1H, CHOH (anti isomer)), 5.06 (t, J=4.2 Hz, 1H, CHOH
(syn isomer)); The enantiomeric ratios were determined by HPLC analysis
(Daicel OD-H column with hexane-i-PrOH=20:1, flow rate=0.6 mL/min):7
tR=17.9 (syn, major enantiomer), 20.2 (anti, major enantiomer), 28.5
(anti, minor enantiomer), 45.7 (syn, minor enantiomer) min.
