$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction of the
Sulfoxides. tert-Butyl
3-Hydroxy-3-[1-(p-tolylsulfinyl)naphth-2-yl]thiopropanoates (15a and
15b). To a solution of 3a (23.7 mg, 0.081 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) was
added BF3·OEt2 (1.34 mol L-1 solution in CH2Cl2, 0.13 mL, 0.174 mmol) at
-78 °C and the mixture was stirred for 1 h. The solution of S-tert-butyl
O-trimethylsilylketene acetal (33.0 mg, 0.161 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL)
was added to the mixture and stirred for 7 h. HCl (1 mol L-1 ) was added
and stirred for 15 min. Usual workup gave the crude product which was
purified by column chromatography (silica gel 10 g, hexane/ethyl
acetate=90:10) to afford 15a (25.2 mg, 74%) and 15b (6.0 mg, 18%). The
diastereomer ratio was determined to be 79:21 by the 1H NMR analysis of
the crude product. tert-Butyl
3-Hydroxy-3-[1-[(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)sulfinyl]naphth-2-yl]thiopropanoates
(16a and 16b). The reaction was carried as described above except using
3b (16.4 mg, 0.051 mmol), BF3·OEt2 (1.34 M solution in CH2Cl2, 0.080 mL,
0.107 mmol,) and S-tert-butyl O- trimethylsilylketene acetal (26.5 mg,
0.130 mmol). Usual workup gave the crude product which was purified by
column chromatography (silica gel 10 g, hexane/ethyl acetate=90:10) to
afford 16 (39.2 mg, 81%). The diastereomer ratio was determined to be
95:5 by the 1H NMR analysis of the crude product. 16a; Rf =0.48
(CH2Cl2/Et2O=95:5); 1H NMR δ 1.47 (s, 9H), 2.21 (dd, 1H, J = 2.2, 16.6
Hz), 2.25 (s, 3H), 2.40 (s, 6H), 2.75 (dd, 1H, J = 9.9, 16.6 Hz), 3.68
(d, 1H, J = 2.7 Hz), 6.03-6.15 (m, 1H), 6.82 (s, 2H), 7.40-7.55 (m, 2H),
7.70-8.00 (m, 3H), 8.85- 9.00 (m, 1H); 13C NMR δ δ 20.1, 22.1, 29.8,
48.5, 51.1, 65.0, 123.8, 124.5, 126.4, 127.0, 128.7, 131.3, 131.4, 131.7,
133.2, 133.5, 138.8, 141.0, 141.8; IR (neat) 3330, 2960, 2920, 1700,
1600, 1460, 1400, 1160, 1080, 1040, 960, 820, 760, 710 cm-1 ; EIMS m/z
(rel intensity) 454 (M+ , 1), 436 (50), 347 (15), 305 (100); Anal. Calcd
for C26H30O3S2: C, 68.69; H, 6.65. Found: C, 68.60; H,. 6.77. 16b; Rf
=0.15 (CH2Cl2/Et2O=95:5); 1H NMR δ 1.44 (s, 9H), 2.25 (s, 3H), 2.35 (s,
6H), 2.48 (dd, 1H, J = 3.5, 15.8 Hz), 2.98 (dd, 1H, J = 9.7, 15.8 Hz),
5.30 (s, 1H), 6.05 (dd, 1H, J = 3.5, 9.7 Hz), 6.80 (s, 2H), 7.40-8.00 (m,
5H), 8.45-8.60 (m, 1H); 13C NMR δ δ 16.9, 19.5, 22.0, 31.3, 53.1, 65.4,
125.0, 127.4, 128.1, 129.0, 129.4, 130.4, 132.1, 133.5, 139.7, 142.5,
144.0, 198.7; IR (neat) 3380, 2980, 2940, 1680, 1450, 1380, 1320, 1120,
1100, 1050 cm-1 ; EIMS m/z (rel intensity) 454 (M+ , 0.2), 436 (70), 305
(100); Anal. Calcd for C26H30O3S2: C, 68.69; H, 6.65. Found: C, 68.47;
H,. 6.81
