$DATUM To a stirred solution of 9 (23mg, 0.045mmol) and enol silane (13mg,
0.082mmol) in 2ml CH2Cl2 was added BF3-EtO2 (6.8mg, 0.048mmol) at -78°C.
Maintain the temperature for 30min then quenched with 1ml aq. NaHCO3,
extracted with ether, dry (Na2SO4) and evaporated to give a residue,
which was subjected to flash column chromatography to provide both (-)-11
(22mg, 81%) and (-)-11a (3mg, 10%) as colorless oil. (-)-11, yield (81%)
22mg; (-)-11a, yield 10%, 3mg. (-)-11: Rf = 0.35 (Hexane : Ethyl acetate
= 5:1); [α ]22 D= -51.35 (c 0.01, CHCl3); IR (thin film, cm-1) 680, 775,
