$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of aldehyde (0.8 mmol) in
propionitrile (0.32 mL) was added over 10 min to a mixed solution of the
silyl enol ether (0.96 mmol) and 2d (0.08 mmol) in propionitrile (0.65
mL). 4,6-Dimethyl-5-hydroxy-3-heptanone (Table 3), yield 94%. 1H NMR, 13C
NMR, and IR spectroscopic data are in agreement with those reported in
the literatures.5 The syn/anti ratio was determined by 1H NMR
spectroscopy: 1H NMR (CDCl3 , 300 MHz) δ 3.39-3.48 (m, 1H, OH (anti
isomer)), 3.48-3.58 (m, 1H, OH (syn isomer)); The enantiomeric ratios and
the absolute configurations were determined by HPLC analysis (two linear
Daicel AD columns with hexane-i-PrOH=200:1, flow rate=1.0 mL/min) of
Mosher esters derived from (+)-MTPA: 56 tR=16.5 (syn, minor enantiomer
(4S,5R)), 21.2 (anti, minor enantiomer (4R,5R)), 22.2 (anti, major
enantiomer (4S,5S)), 24.6 (syn, major enantiomer (4R,5S)) min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
