$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for t BuOK-Catalyzed VMA Reaction of TMSOF with
Aldehydes t BuOK (0.025 M) in THF (20 μL, 0.1 mmol%) was added to a
solution of aldehyde (0.25 mmol) and TMSOF (0.3 mmol) in 1.0mL
tetrahydrofuran (THF) was added at 0°C. The reaction mixture was stirred
at rt until the starting aldehyde was consumed as indicated by thin-layer
chromatography (TLC). The solution was then cooled to 0°C and quenched
with 10% aqueous HCl. The mixture was stirred for 30 min, neutralized by
saturated aqueous NaHCO3, and then extrated with ethyl acetate. The
combined organic phase was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The ratio of anti/syn was determined by 1H NMR analysis of
the crude products, and the configurations were assigned by 1H NMR
comparison with literature. The crude products were purified through
silica-gel chromatography (ethyl acetate-petroleum ether). Pure
anti-products or a mixture of anti/syn isomers.
5-((4-Chlorophenyl)(hydroxyl)methyl)furan-2(5H)-one (3a).[6a] Compound 3a
was prepared according to the general procedure and purified by
chromatography on silica gel (PE-EtOAc, 4:1). 3a as the pure
anti-diastereoisomer, white solid (93%), anti/syn c - 84:16. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.42-7.28 (m, 5H), 6.11 (dd, J=6.0, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.18-5.10
(m, 1H), 5.03 (t, J=4.0 Hz, 1H), 3.93 (d, J=3.6 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ 173.5, 153.1, 136.9, 134.1, 128.8, 127.6, 123.2, 86.7,
72.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, optimization study, optimized
on catalyst concentration,solvent and temperature in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diastereoselective synthesis of γ-butenolides catalyzed by potassium
tert-butoxide
